sysmon (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Settings are now per user in ~/.config/sysmon/sysmon.ini and can be
    edited with File -> Settings; changes apply immediately. An existing
    /etc/sysmon.ini is copied to the per-user file once, and the package
    no longer creates /etc/sysmon.ini.
  * Built-in defaults are worked out from the hardware at every start:
    lo is hidden, mmcblk0 is hidden when the root filesystem is on NVMe,
    and eth0 is hidden on an Argon ONE UP.
  * [smartctl] settings are limited to "-d TYPE", since smartctl runs as
    root.
  * Taller charts: titles are drawn inside the charts (click to collapse),
    less padding, legends on the right with a shared width so the time
    axes line up.
  * Ship the application icon at 16-256 px as well as SVG.
  * Help -> Repository now opens https://github.com/JeffCurless/sysmon;
    removed Help -> Configuration Help.

 -- Jeff Curless <jeff@thecurlesses.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:33:38 -0500

sysmon (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

